WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.8 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Accountability and reporting lines

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Accountability starts with the people you serve and your first supporters, long before a board or funders.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
Accountability means being answerable for what you do and what results from it. In purpose-led work it runs in several directions, starting with the people you serve and your first supporters.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
Three directions

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:38.241
Upward: To a board, funders, investors and regulators: results, finance and risk. For example: Our bakery sends the local youth fund a short report on results and spending.

6
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:49.570
Sideways: To partners and peers who share the work or rely on you. For example: The bakery tells the youth centre each month how its referred trainees are doing.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:01:01.730
Downward: To the people you serve: useful information, feedback and decisions explained. For example: The bakery shares trainee survey results with the trainees and says what will change.

8
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:02.730
Why it matters

9
00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:09.144
1. Trust grows when people see what you do with their time and money.

10
00:01:09.144 --> 00:01:15.189
2. Habits built now are easier than adding them once you are busy.

11
00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:21.493
3. Problems surface early when people can raise them without fear.

12
00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:22.493
What it guides

13
00:01:22.493 --> 00:01:28.167
1. Your reporting rhythm: what you report, to whom and how often.

14
00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:33.100
2. Your feedback with communities, developed further in Module 6.

15
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:39.404
3. Your check-ins: clear expectations and fair consequences, among co-founders too.

16
00:01:39.804 --> 00:01:40.404
What to avoid

17
00:01:40.404 --> 00:01:45.337
Reporting only upward and forgetting the people you serve.

18
00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:50.270
Expectations between co-founders that are never said or reviewed.

19
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:56.204
Blaming people when things go wrong instead of learning.

20
00:01:56.804 --> 00:01:58.604
You map your accountability lines and first-year reporting rhythm.

21
00:01:58.604 --> 00:02:02.604
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:07.204
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
